{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Manages the public key on a peer's user record and how it was obtained (key_source: offline | vouched | tofu | verified). action set pins the given 64-hex publickey as an offline-exchanged key (replacing any other; live connections are dropped when it differs); verify marks the key on record as checked by the user; forget removes the key so the next contact starts over (drops live connections); lookup asks every connected peer that may vouch (an admin here, or one already holding all of the target's groups) for the key through peer.info and pins it when the record has none. Returns FLAT {status, id, publickey?, key_source?, key_voucher?, disconnected?, lookup? {asked, answered, found, conflict}}. Also the home of the shared helpers valid_key, stamp, drop_connections, can_vouch, apply_vouch and vouch_lookup used by peer.service.maintenance and the handshakes. Admin-only.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse crate::security::security::init::{get_user, set_user, secure_id};\nuse crate::security::security::users::users;\nuse crate::peer::service::listen::{P2PConnection, get_best, to_hex};\nuse crate::peer::service::exec::exec;\nuse flowlang::blake2b::Blake2b;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;\nuse std::thread;\nuse std::sync::mpsc;\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n","params":[{"desc":"UUID of the peer whose key record to change. The peer must already be a local user record.","name":"uuid","type":"String"},{"desc":"set = pin the given publickey as an offline-exchanged key (replaces any other key and drops that peer's live connections when it differs); verify = mark the key already on record as checked by the user; forget = remove the key so the next contact starts over (drops live connections); lookup = ask connected, eligible peers for this peer's key and pin it when the record has none.","name":"action","type":"String"},{"desc":"64 hex digits. Required for set. For verify it may carry the key the user was looking at (refused if the record has since changed) or be empty. Pass an empty string for forget and lookup.","name":"publickey","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"xsjxyj1a1f8e3c8bej1","readers":[],"time":1795177071463,"username":"system","writers":[]}